DESCRIPTION Triage band, scan Warning-level events over a window and summarize the most concerning; honest 'none concerning', no fabricated events.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "Are there any Warning-level Kubernetes events in the last hour? Summarize
  the most concerning ones."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)


# Reference-grounded quality, deferred LLM judge (FitnessCrew) scores the
# synthesis 0.0-1.0 against this ground truth from cluster-ground-truth-baseline.md.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "Checks cluster-wide Warning-level Kubernetes events over the window and summarizes the most concerning. The correct answer is whatever Warning events the live events API holds in the window at the time of the question: it reports the real recurring or recent Warnings it finds (for example a failing image repository scan, a node reporting NotReady or becoming unschedulable, FailedScheduling for a pod, or a container restart) with the object, reason and message as the live events show them, and ranks them by concern. When the window holds no Warning events, the correct answer is a plain none. A confident all-clear built on an empty or NO_DATA query result when real Warnings exist misses them, and an event, object, reason or count that the live events do not show is fabrication.")
